by Kocal at 2026-10-11T06:07:21Z

I pushed a change on top of this. Skipping the `X-Live-Url` update when the Navigation API history entry key changed broke one case: jumping to an in-page anchor (`#section`) also creates a new history entry, so the key changes even though the user stays on the same page. I checked this behavior in Chromium. Before this PR, the URL was still updated in that case, so this needed a fix.

Now, when the key changed, the URL is still updated if the path and query string are the same as when the request was sent. I added a test for the anchor case, and updated the "history entry changed" test to also change the URL, like a real Turbo visit or a back/forward navigation would. Without that, the test looks like the same page under the new rule and no longer exercises the skip.

Commit message and PR description are updated to match.
